Z||000010||DRH||01-20-2000||01:55 PM||||Hey Nut (or is that Mr. Nut?),<P>Spotted a Formula in the parking lot at work today. I'll have to find out who belongs to it. Kinda wierd since I haven't seen it here before and it just snowed 4-6 inches. Not sure why they brought a fairly low mile car out in the snow and salt??? <P>Here's the info:<BR>1G2PE1190JP202899<BR>Formula, Bright Red, Auto, AC, CC, PW, 42k, nice shape in and out.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||88 Database Nut||01-20-2000||04:04 PM||||That's "Hey You!" to you!  I'll answer to most anything, especially when you add the word VIN to it...<P>Good Work sir, I had gotten this car from an add on 1/26/99, but didn't have the color or any other info. Thanks for filling in the details.  It was for sale in West Union, IA.<BR>Wonder how it wound up in 4-6 inches of snow in Wisconsin?<P>Many thanks, it's always nice to get the details and the fact that it's still rotating it's tires!||||reg||14
Z||000012||DRH||01-20-2000||04:19 PM||||West Union, IA is only 85 mile from here. I think I've seen it around town (or another just like it) except now it's got the 14" rims instead of the 15" (of course mine does too, better tires in case I HAVE to drive in snow). First time I've seen it at work though...<P>Did you get my other reply just above that one?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||88 Database Nut||01-20-2000||04:26 PM||||Yes I Did!  Sorry if I didn't email you and say thanks!  Say, the car built right after yours is owned by someone in Maine, it's also Black, with Grey interior, and is a Factory TTop (it's a coupe).<BR>Right now we're at 929 cars.  I'll email you the summary sheet after I right this.<P>Thanks Again, I do appreciate everybody's help.  I'd be lost without y'all.<P>John||||reg||7
Z||000014||Carrolles||01-20-2000||04:33 PM||||I found this 88 T-Top Coupe in a junk yard in Augusta, GA.  The T-tops are missing and the car has been pretty much stripped although it still has the 4cyl engine, transmission, and suspension.  Seats are gone as well as the shifter and cables and wheels.  The windshield is smashed and the driver's side windshield frame is slightly bent. The driver's side rear corner trim piece at the roof opening is missing.  The courtesy light fixture is there and the headliner is there although the fabric is hanging since the car is out in the weather with no tops.<P>I asked for a price to have them cut the top off at the lower end of the windshield posts and about midway down the rear pillars.  $200.00 including any of the trim that goes with it and the weatherstripping around the door openings (fair shape).  $500.00 gets the whold car as it sits with no title.<P>It is located at Craven Auto (706) 790-6365.<P>VIN  1G2PE11R3JP201892||||reg||1
Z||000015||88 Database Nut||01-20-2000||04:39 PM||||Wow, thanks for the info.  $200 seems pretty fair for all that, considering you can probably get $1000 for the whole kit if you remove it neatly.  You can goto fiero.net and then the link to the ttop site, where there are detailed drawings of the assembly of the ttops.  Should make the dis-assembly fairly easy.  <BR>Thanks very much for this info. I'm heading out the door but will add it tomorrow and send you a summary.  Wish Augusta was a little closer to Atlanta.  You weren't able to see a body color, were you?  Should be either Bright Red or White from the cars around it in the database.  I'll check to see if this is a factory TTop car, so I can let Ray Paulk know about it (he runs the TTop Registry at the above site).<BR>Take Care, Thanks Again,<P>John||||reg||1
