Z||000018||DRH||01-21-2000||02:54 PM||||Spyder, Ouch  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>What's the story? Looks like the body skin is basically still there... seems like it would melt and/or burn...<p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 01-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Spyder||01-21-2000||03:29 PM||||Here is what happened to my 88, I had it at my father in-laws shop, I was taking the 5 speed out for my 84 v8 project and I was going to put the 4 speed into the 88. During a long holiday weekend someone broke into my car and torched it. They also broke into a few other cars.  His shop also caught fire, the fire fighters put it out before too much damage.  The transaxle was taken out two days earlier.  The bad news was, I didn’t have insurance and neither did he.<BR>What looks like body panels on the burnt car is actually just single strands of fiber in a mesh, when I went to lift the hood  the small portion in my hand just pulled right off. <P>Here is the “Before” picture: (The picture quality isn’t that good.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.mindspring.com/~mm889-19/fiero.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mindspring.com/~mm889-19/fierofire.jpg"> <BR>The fire fighters said it was billowing black-black smoke.  It was so hot that the glass melted, and then cooled into some really neat shapes. <P><BR>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 01-22-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 01-22-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000020||88 Database Nut||01-21-2000||03:38 PM||||Gees Spyder, that's a sad tale.  I don't want to sound like a ghoul, but if you still had an insurance card or something I would like to have the VIN from your car, so I can add it to the list of cars which are "deceased".<P>That has to be one of the worst experiences one can have with a car.  I hope you have much better luck with your future cars.<P>Take care, Have a Good Weekend,<P>John Willhoff, Marietta GA (aka Database Nut)||||reg||9
Z||000021||DRH||01-21-2000||03:57 PM||||Spyder, Brush what's left of the skin off and market it as a kit car donor.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Seriously, that is a shame... it was a nice looking car.<P>||||reg||1
